The coordination procedure is changed and recorded as a project memory that both coordinators concur on (TermAl and Engram), with these rules:
(1) a drain for an operator act starts only after Greg's own explicit readiness reply through Asistant;
(2) the operator instructions go through BOTH Asistant and Advisor;
(3) the coordinator sets a one-time check for the agreed start plus 15 minutes. If there's no evidence then (the host-lifecycle record, the installed binary hash, a backup or log, or Greg's reply), it lifts the hold and tells every lane, without waiting for a message.
